{%- comment -%}
  GVM Packages Grid -- shared content, rendered by sections/gvm-packages-grid.liquid
  on every page that uses it (currently: page.gvm-hub-vehicles.json and
  page.b2b-catalog.json). Editing THIS file updates both pages at once --
  that's the whole point of it being a snippet instead of section blocks.

  Images are the one exception: Shopify's image_picker settings only
  resolve inside a section's own settings, so they're passed in as
  parameters from the section rather than referenced directly here.
  Everything else (titles, text, links) is set here, so making a hub
  live -- e.g. once the F150/Tundra/Silverado 2500 pages exist -- is a
  single edit: replace its '#' with the hub URL and the card switches
  from "Coming soon" to a link on its own (snippets/ori-vehicle-card.liquid).

  Params expected: image_f150, image_tundra, image_silverado1500,
  image_silverado2500 (Image objects from the section's settings).
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="ori-vgrid">
  {%- render 'ori-vehicle-card',
    title: 'Ford F150 GVM Packages',
    text: 'Click here to learn more about ORI GVM GCM packages for the Ford F150',
    url: '#',
    image: image_f150
  -%}
  {%- render 'ori-vehicle-card',
    title: 'Toyota Tundra GVM Packages',
    text: 'Click here to learn more about ORI GVM GCM packages for the Toyota Tundra',
    url: '#',
    image: image_tundra
  -%}
  {%- render 'ori-vehicle-card',
    title: 'Chevy Silverado 1500 GVM Packages',
    text: 'Click here to learn more about ORI GVM GCM packages for the Chevy Silverado 1500',
    url: '/collections/chevrolet-silverado-1500-ltz-zr2-trailboss-gvm-upgrade',
    image: image_silverado1500
  -%}
  {%- render 'ori-vehicle-card',
    title: 'Chevy Silverado 2500HD GVM Packages',
    text: 'Click here to learn more about ORI GVM GCM packages for the Chevy Silverado 2500HD',
    url: '#',
    image: image_silverado2500
  -%}
</div>
